i've got to say up front this wasn't my  favorite episode of for all mankind  i guess it's inevitable in a story with  so many things going on but i didn't  find myself interested in a lot of what  unfolded here  that said it did have some great moments  a latest celebration at jsc  gordo's son finding him in the closet  with his helmet on  and then karen ruthlessly spoiling the  wrathicon for  ed those are all things i'm gonna  remember hey guys pete here  this is my for all mankind season 2  episode 5 breakdown  the episode was titled the weight  w-e-i-g-h-t  although it did feel a little bit more  like the weight w-a-i-t  to me just a quick spoiler warning if  you haven't watched the episode yet this  video will  absolutely spoil it and with that out of  the way let's get right to it  the opening of this episode was  absolutely amazing though  tracy's on the moon we see this glorious  sequence where she comes down the stairs  looks around at the surface is  completely odd  and then we learned that her cameraman  forgot to hit record  so she has to do it all again it's  definitely one of the high points of the  episode  and the fact that she has to go back and  redo it to recapture that feeling of  inspiration  does work well for where her time on the  moon goes  i wish it just could have been a little  bit more fun to watch we see  a lot of moon time in this episode and  we also see that she is the rock star of  the bunch  this sets her apart from the other  people there kind of isolates her  but at the same time she's on tv she's  talking to johnny carson  which all works to make it kind of hard  to feel bad for  a couple of things that stand out here  though the old linus  the other new guy that was there just  before her tells her how he remembers  watching her save molly's life on tv  and how he's always looked up to her for  it and that serves as a good reminder  because  tracy's struggle in the first season was  that no one thought she was up to the  task  now in this episode we see that that  struggle has shifted  in the direction of she's kinda getting  everything that she wanted but it  doesn't appear to be making her happy  and that comes out explicitly when she  goes to visit deke's grave at the end  so we see her struggle with that we see  that she can't sleep she starts drinking  she blocks the air vent in her bunk that  leads to an alarm going off  and pissing everybody off including her  commander  and overall in her first month things  are not going well  and she's got five more to go so we're  gonna see things change for her going  forward  no more tv interviews no more special  treatment  the other thing we see is that she can  fly the lsam  she's still a good pilot so we'll see  where they take things from here  in baldwin land karen gets the call that  ed's plane went down  we see her with kelly she's waiting to  find out what happened  she's a nervous wreck understandably and  eventually they get the call that he's  alright  and she makes a point of telling kelly  this is what it's like for the people  you love  and you should know that when ed comes  home in the morning  we see that he's beat up from the  ejection but the doctor said he'll be  all right  karen puts up a facade pretending like  she doesn't care  everything is fine and she's just going  to go to work at 6 00 a.m  because everything's fine and of course  ed and kelly can see through this but  that's the way she's dealing with things  there's really no progress in this later  we see at the outpost danny kelly and  karen are all eating together  and when ed shows up everything is still  pretty awkward  danny leaves kelly goes back to work and  karen still doesn't really want to hang  out with that at all  as i mentioned in the beginning she  makes sure to spoil rather khan for him  when he asks her to go  because she's already seen it with kelly  at the end of the episode we see karen  and danny have a conversation at the  outpost  he tells her memories about coming over  to the house when he was a kid  brings up the fact that he saw her  dancing by herself to elvis in the  living room when she didn't know he was  there  and then they talk about shane something  that they both have that ties them  together  they both still really miss shane after  they talk we see karen go home put on an  elvis record and dance by herself in the  living room  as far as consequences for what ed and  gordo did  there are none really watching margot  molly and payne  listening to their tape of them doing  the dogfight was hilarious though  but yeah i mean big surprise molly takes  their side  she's pretty firm about it backing up  the other astronauts and  not sure if that's going to lead to  something else down the road  the only other thing with molly in this  episode is we see her talking to the  astronauts who are taking the guns up to  the moon  it's an important development we've been  waiting for this to happen  but it's kind of just sandwiched in  there and the main thing in relation to  molly  is that we see that our eyesight is  failing and that could be  related to what happened to or being  exposed to radiation on the moon  for what it's worth we do see the guns  arrive so they are there  at jamestown base but we have to wait  until later to see what the reaction is  down the road  gordo does seem to be taking things  seriously at this point  we see that he's still struggling inside  the helmet but he's trying to do what he  can  at home to get over the fear we got a  little bit of a montage of him like a  training montage where he's getting  himself back into shape  throwing his liquor bottles away so it's  hinting that he's on the road to  redemption  we also see elena show up for her first  day of work at nasa  i mentioned i really liked how she did  the whole screaming behind the  soundproof glass thing it felt like a  triumph  we see that she's excited this is a  dream that's realized  and is confirmed that she is working on  the apollo soyuz  project which is the one where danielle  is going to be meeting with the russians  for the handshake in space  and we see her have this awkward  exchange where she's being asked  questions about her background and she  really doesn't want to talk about it  it makes you think there are multiple  reasons why she wouldn't want to get  into her background  and it's kind of interesting to see  where that goes  when i was first watching it i was  thinking like maybe she  is socially awkward like extremely  socially awkward in these kind of things  but it really makes more sense that  since her father was deported  that she has a strained relationship  with margot  who also did her a big favor putting her  in this position  that she might just really not want to  explain how she got there  it seems like they're setting her up to  do something  in relation to this project figure  something out make a name for herself  it's certainly the trajectory you would  expect her story to take  so i'm hoping that we'll get to learn a  little bit more about where she's been  at for the last nine years  what's really going on with her getting  fired from all these places  because that doesn't just happen for no  reason right  and then i guess the last big story of  this episode  was ellen and pam reuniting she goes to  see her at a poetry reading  pam is living with a partner she's in  austin so she's out  she's not closeted like she was when she  was with ellen  she seems happy she tries to play it off  that she's excited to see ellen  and there's a couple fake outs here  where you think that they're not gonna  hook back up but at the end of the day  they do  and it is good to see that pam's back  that would have been a loss if she just  disappeared from the story but again  this kind of just felt like it was  sandwiched in there among all the other  things happening  seeing them back together would  certainly make you think that she's  going to end up making their  relationship  public of course she could go the sally  ride route  and never explain it until after she  dies  but you can't really see pam coming back  into her life unless that happens  there's really only two options here  ellen quits nasa and she goes to austin  and they live together there  or ellen comes out and pam and her get  together publicly  and they deal with the fallout and  that's pretty much everything that  happened  that's the big stuff so yeah my least  favorite episode of the season so far  still not my least favorite episode of  tv i've watched recently  and there were some of my favorite  little moments thrown in there  i guess a lot of it has to do with me  not feeling that interested in tracy's  story right now  and it's not because she's a bad  character really it's just that there's  so many other things going on  and this was one of my big problems with  the first season of this show  you have all these interesting things  going on side by side but they don't  always  work well together it's interesting when  you step back and think about it tracy  is kind of the rock star right  if ed had gone back if gordo hadn't lost  his mind  molly isn't inclined to go looking for  that kind of attention  any one of them could have been the rock  star because the space program is  popular in that timeline  but when you think about it like that  then yeah of course tracy is a good  candidate for that but it's not  something endearing necessarily  and then like i said it's kind of hard  to feel bad for her because  she's got a pretty good life it's all  probably leading to something  i think in the case of what's going on  with tracy right now  and what's going on with karen right now  i just don't find myself wondering how  they're going to get through it or what  is the kind of ending or the kind of  thing i want to see happen to them  right now in this part of the story with  ellen it's more cut and dry you know you  want to see your get together with pam  if that's what they're going to do you'd  like to see her be able to be who she is  have a fulfilling life she certainly  earned that  she's certainly good at her job and all  that so it's a little more cut and dry  in that situation  i am curious to see what's going to  happen with elena it's a pretty nice  touch that she's been  around jsc enough as a child through a  relationship with her father and with  margo  that she knows enough when she goes into  the observation room that no one can  hear her and she just goes ahead and  cuts  loose but as she was in that  conversation i did think about the fact  that she's been fired  everywhere else that she's worked and  it's clear that working at nasa  is important to her this is her lifelong  dream right so  definitely some potential there and i  think that's a good place to leave it  we'll see where things go next week let  me know in the comments what you think  what you're hoping to see next and you  know we're halfway there now so  things should be picking up as we go  into the back half please like this  video if you enjoyed it please subscribe  to my channel if you haven't already  thanks for watching i'll talk to you  soon

